{"name":"Clary Sage","hex":"#c7c0ce","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"clary sage","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Salvia sclarea, a biennial or short-lived herbaceous perennial."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clary_sage"}],"entries":[{"title":"Salvia sclarea","blocks":[{"text":"Salvia sclarea, the clary or clary sage, is a biennial (short-lived) herbaceous perennial in the genus Salvia. It is native to the northern Mediterranean Basin and to some areas in north Africa and Central Asia. The plant has long been cultivated as an herb and is currently grown for its essential oil."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Salvia_sclarea3.jpg/330px-Salvia_sclarea3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salvia_sclarea"},{"title":"Sage (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Sage is a grey-green resembling that of dried sage leaves. As a quaternary color, it is an equal mix of the tertiary colors citron and slate. The hex RGB color value of the adjacent sage swatch is BCB88A. For decades, some military flight jackets were made in sage green."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Sage_iPhone_17.jpg/330px-Sage_iPhone_17.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sage_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Sauge_sclar%C3%A9e.jpg/500px-Sauge_sclar%C3%A9e.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Sauge_sclar%C3%A9e.jpg/1280px-Sauge_sclar%C3%A9e.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Sauge_sclar%C3%A9e.jpg/500px-Sauge_sclar%C3%A9e.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnai